%N A401848 Trajectory of 30 under the map x -> x^(omega(x)-1) + 1, where omega(x) is the number of distinct prime divisors of x.
%C A401848 If omega(x) = 1, the next term is 2, and the orbit stabilizes at 2. If omega(x) >= 2, the next term is greater than x; if the orbit never encounters a prime power, it is strictly increasing and unbounded.
%C A401848 Conjecture: For every integer k >= 2, the orbit starting at k eventually reaches 2.
%C A401848 The orbit starting from n = 30 generates at least 9 terms without encountering a prime power.
%C A401848 a(9) has 1242 digits.
%F A401848 a(1) = 30, a(n+1) = a(n)^(A001221(a(n))-1) + 1.
%t A401848 NestList[#^(PrimeNu[#] - 1) + 1 &, 30, 7] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 15 2026 *)
%o A401848 (Python)
%o A401848 from sympy.ntheory import primefactors
%o A401848 x = 30
%o A401848 terms = [x]
%o A401848 for _ in range(6):
%o A401848     w = len(primefactors(x))
%o A401848     x = x**(w - 1) + 1
%o A401848     terms.append(x)
%o A401848 print(", ".join(map(str, terms)))
%Y A401848 Cf. A001221, A246655.
%K A401848 nonn,new
%O A401848 1,1
%A A401848 _Nguyen Trong Nhan_, Nov 07 2026
